# Apt package list for the consolidated image, factored out of the Dockerfile.
# One package per line; "#" starts a comment and blank lines are ignored.
# The Dockerfile installs everything listed here in a single apt transaction.
#
# This is the union of the package sets of docker-stacks-foundation,
# base-notebook, and minimal-notebook (see the group headers below) and the
# apt-install calls in science-platform-images deployments/common/Dockerfile,
# deduplicated:
#   - sudo is intentionally NOT installed: the common layer removed it ("hub
#     users cannot use, security risk"), so here we simply never add it.
#   - vim-tiny was replaced by full vim (the common layer installed vim).
#   - ssh (metapackage) and openssh-client collapsed into openssh-server
#     (which depends on openssh-client for git-over-ssh).

# --- from docker-stacks-foundation ---
ca-certificates
locales
# - `netbase` provides /etc/{protocols,rpc,services}, part of POSIX
#   and required by various C functions like getservbyname and getprotobyname
#   https://github.com/jupyter/docker-stacks/pull/2129
netbase
# - `tini` is installed as a helpful container entrypoint,
#   that reaps zombie processes and such of the actual executable we want to start
#   See https://github.com/krallin/tini#why-tini for details
tini
wget

# --- from base-notebook ---
# - Add necessary fonts for matplotlib/seaborn
#   See https://github.com/jupyter/docker-stacks/pull/380 for details
fonts-liberation
# - `pandoc` is used to convert notebooks to html files
#   it's not present in the aarch64 Ubuntu image, so we install it here
pandoc
# - `run-one` - a wrapper script that runs no more
#   than one unique instance of some command with a unique set of arguments,
#   we use `run-one-constantly` to support the `RESTARTABLE` option
run-one

# --- from minimal-notebook: OS dependencies for a fully functional Server ---
# Common useful utilities
curl
git
nano-tiny
tzdata
unzip
# `less` is needed to run help in R
# see: https://github.com/jupyter/docker-stacks/issues/1588
less
# `nbconvert` dependencies
# https://nbconvert.readthedocs.io/en/latest/install.html#installing-tex
texlive-xetex
texlive-fonts-recommended
texlive-plain-generic
# Enable clipboard on Linux host systems
xclip

# --- from common: base utilities ---
apt-utils
openssl
vim

# --- from common: misc system tools ---
tree
rsync
groff
htop
sysstat
net-tools
rename
stress-ng
# GUI libraries (e.g. for headless browser / desktop-server use)
libxcomposite1
libxdamage1
libgtk-3-0t64
libatk1.0-0t64

# --- from common: S/W development tools ---
build-essential
gfortran
automake
libtool
make
cmake
emacs-nox
libfftw3-dev
libatlas-base-dev
libcurl4-openssl-dev
libxml2
libxml2-dev
libxslt1.1
libxslt1-dev
graphviz
libopenblas-dev
zlib1g-dev
jq
# git-over-ssh (openssh-server pulls in openssh-client)
openssh-server

# --- from common: libraries for FITS, DS9, ML ---
file
libcfitsio-bin
libcfitsio-dev
apt-file
libxpa-dev
libxt-dev
libbz2-dev
